# Buffered and ranged streams with AzureSDK

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:azure_sdk, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Overview

`upload_stream/5` stages Put Block chunks (default 4 MiB) and commits with Put
Block List. `download_stream/4` fetches the blob with HTTP Range requests.

Requires Azurite (`docker compose up -d`).

```elixir
credential =
  AzureSDK.Identity.SharedKeyCredential.new(
    "devstoreaccount1",
    "Eby8vdM02xNOcqFlqUwJPLlmEtlCDXJ1OUzFT50uSRZ6IFsuFq2UVErCz4I6tq/K1SZFPTOtr/KBHBeksoGMGw=="
  )

client =
  AzureSDK.Storage.Client.new(
    account: "devstoreaccount1",
    credential: credential,
    endpoint: "http://127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1"
  )

container = "stream-demo"

unless AzureSDK.Storage.Container.exists?(client, container) do
  {:ok, _} = AzureSDK.Storage.Container.create(client, container)
end

:ok
```

## Stream upload

```elixir
stream = Stream.repeatedly(fn -> "chunk-data-" end) |> Stream.take(20)

{:ok, _} =
  AzureSDK.Storage.Blob.upload_stream(client, container, "chunks.bin", stream,
    block_size: 32
  )

:ok
```

## Stream download

```elixir
{:ok, stream} =
  AzureSDK.Storage.Blob.download_stream(client, container, "chunks.bin", chunk_size: 64)

stream |> Enum.join() |> byte_size()
```

## Clean up

```elixir
{:ok, :deleted} = AzureSDK.Storage.Blob.delete(client, container, "chunks.bin")
{:ok, :deleted} = AzureSDK.Storage.Container.delete(client, container)
:ok
```
